Reject non-``str`` ``name`` arguments to :meth:`Component.add <icalendar.cal.component.Component.add>` with a clear :class:`TypeError`. Previously, ``Calendar().add(123, "hello")`` or ``Calendar().add(None, "hello")`` would pass through the type-validation layer and crash inside the property factory with ``AttributeError: 'int' object has no attribute 'upper'`` (or ``'NoneType'``), which looked like a library bug. The new error message names the offending type and includes the value so a user passing the wrong argument from a dict lookup or a JSON loader gets a clear, immediate error at the call site instead.
